\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {IV}{\ignorespaces Success rate (\%) by benchmark, magnitude, and redundancy condition. Smart, Global, and Combined succeed via constrained LGP planning (Combined merges every object's goal into a single monolithic terminal instead of decomposing the task); VLM-MSGraph~\cite  {li2025vlm} is evaluated by whether its naive interpolation executes without collision, given the same scenes and task assignment. Cube stacking: N=1000 (Smart/Global), N=500 (VLM-MSGraph), N=100 at four cubes / not executed at five--eight cubes (Combined, see text). FMB: N=50 per cell (Smart/Global/Combined, no exclusions -- re-run with no wall-clock timeout, 16GB memory cap only), N=300 (VLM-MSGraph).}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:planning_sr}{{IV}{10}{}{table.4}{}}
